# Titlebar Component Patterns

## Platform-Aware Rendering

Always use `detectPlatform()` or the `platform` prop. Never check `navigator.userAgent` directly:

```typescript
import { OS } from '~/utils';

function detectPlatform(): Platform {
  if (OS.isMacOS()) return 'macos';
  if (OS.isLinux()) return 'linux';
  return 'windows';
}

const platform = platformOverride ?? detectPlatform();
```

## Discriminated Union Props

Use discriminated unions for mutually exclusive modes:

```typescript
// GOOD
type WithButtons = { macOnly?: false; handleClose(): void; handleMinus(): void };
type MacOnly = { macOnly: true; handleClose?: never; handleMinus?: never };
type Props = WithButtons | MacOnly;
```

## Sub-Component Layout

WindowControls orchestrates all sub-components in order:

```
WindowControls
├── Menu              (dropdown menu bar)
├── Title             (centered title / drag region)
├── SearchBar         (command palette trigger + overlay)
├── ToolbarActions    (action buttons: icon + filled/split)
├── UserProfile       (avatar + dropdown)
└── [!macOnly] ButtonContainer (minimize, maximize, close)
```

Both macOS and non-macOS branches render Menu, SearchBar, ToolbarActions, UserProfile identically. Only window control buttons differ.

## New Props Flow

Props flow from Titlebar -> WindowControls -> sub-components:

```
Titlebar (actions, renderActions, user, commandPalette, menuItems)
  └── WindowControls (receives all above via props)
        ├── Menu (menuItems, platform)
        ├── SearchBar (commandPalette, platform)
        ├── ToolbarActions (actions, renderActions)
        └── UserProfile (user, userActions, onSignIn, onSignOut)
```

## Type Exports

All public types must be re-exported from `Titlebar.tsx`:

```typescript
export type { TitlebarAction, TitlebarActionDropdownItem, ToolbarActionsProps } from './components/ToolbarActions';
export type { MenuItem, SubMenuItem, MenuItemAction } from './components/Menu';
export type { UserInfo, UserProfileAction, UserStatus } from './components/UserProfile';
export type { CommandPaletteConfig, CommandPaletteSection, ... } from './components/SearchBar';
```

## Testing

- Tests use vitest + jsdom. Auto-detection defaults to `'windows'`.
- Use the `platform` prop to test specific platform layouts.
- Integration tests (Titlebar.test.tsx) verify components render at the top level.
- Unit tests (per component) verify detailed behavior: clicks, dropdowns, keyboard, a11y.
- After changes: `npx vitest run` from `libs/electron-titlebar`.
- Current count: 284 tests across 12 files.
